[l_english.STATE_LORE_502]
Tatzlwurms are creatures that live perpetually underground, preferring to conceal the vents of their subterranean kingdom with gigantic flowers and foliage. Unfortunately, curious ponies often become interested in these peculiar blooms, uprooting them to display, sell, gift, or simply boast about them. Such reckless offenses inevitably provoke the Tatzlwurms’ retaliation, but the unexpected ferocity of this vengeance often leaves ponies too overwhelmed to ponder the reason for their suffering.
Years have passed since the last traveler brought a Tatzlwurm flower back to Equestria; before that, it was perhaps a decade or more. For the record, a not so complete coincident: Equestria’s Ministry of Health records show that the last widespread outbreak of the “Green Flu” occurred years ago, with the one before that dating back perhaps a decade or more. Most ponies have little recollection of the “Green Flu”. A few who witnessed its symptoms and survived blame it on “green-skinned ponies from the West, like demonic plague carriers”. Thus, whenever old pains fade again, houses rise from ruins again, and market cries fill the air again, opportunistic florists invariably embark on westward expeditions.

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_502]
塔佐蠕虫是一种常年生活在地下的生物，它们喜欢用巨型的花朵枝叶遮盖洞穴的通风口，并在地下构筑一个隐秘的王国。只可惜，常常有好事者对那些新奇的花卉感兴趣，将它们连根拔起带回去展示、售卖、赠送、或仅仅是吹嘘。如此鲁莽的冒犯行为一定会招致塔佐蠕虫的报复，但这种报复超乎想象的猛烈程度也容易让小马们来不及关注遭到报复的原因。
距离上一次有旅者将塔佐蠕虫的花带回小马利亚，已经过去了数年，再上一次可能就要追溯到十几年前了；一个不那么完全的巧合的是，小马利亚卫生部门档案中上一次对于“绿色流感”大规模流行的记录发生在数年前，在上一次是十几年前。多数小马对“绿色流感”并没有什么印象，少数目睹过那些病症并依然存活的小马则会将它归咎于“来自西部、通体绿色的小马，宛如恶魔般的瘟疫使者”。因此，每当旧日的痛苦焚烧殆尽，废墟上的房屋重新竖起，市场上的叫卖声络绎不绝时，总还是会有投机的花卉商马踏上向西的考察旅程。
